/-!
# Equations for solvable overgroups of the positive E₆ minuscule subgroup

Over an algebraically closed field, let a reduced, geometrically connected, geometrically solvable
closed subgroup of `GL₂₇` contain the positive subgroup generated by the six positive numbered
root subgroups and the weight torus. Lie--Kolchin gives it an invariant full flag. Its
subcomodules are coordinate spans, because the weight torus separates the twenty-seven minuscule
lines, and they are closed under raising steps, because the positive root subgroups act. A raising
path from `a` to `b` exists exactly when `μ b - μ a` lies in the positive root cone. Hence
every matrix entry `(a, b)` with `μ b - μ a` a nonzero element of that cone vanishes in the
coordinate algebra of the overgroup, so these equations hold on points over arbitrary value
algebras. Consequently the adjoint representation of the overgroup, restricted to the weight
torus, has zero weight space at every nonzero negative-cone character, in every characteristic.

The same conclusions hold for such overgroups inside the carrier generated over the field, in
particular for Borel candidates containing the positive subgroup: the quotient isomorphism
identifies their stored weight tori and adjoint weight spaces. These are the constraints from
which maximality of the positive subgroup among connected solvable subgroups is to be derived.
Neither that maximality nor a comparison with the integral carrier is asserted here.

## References

* J. E. Humphreys, *Linear Algebraic Groups*, §§17 and 21.
* The argument and its statements follow the type-`E₇` construction in
  `TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.E7.Minuscule.Generated.Positive.SolvableOvergroup`.
  `Comodule.exists_basis_coefficientMatrix_isUpperTriangular_of_geometricallySolvable` supplies
  the stable flag, and `HopfIdeal.adjointWeightSpace_eq_bot_of_weightTorusCoordinateBialgHom`
  turns the vanishing of matrix entries into the vanishing of adjoint weight spaces.
-/

public section

